The binning test (Table~\ref{tab:binning}) separates cadence from noise averaging. Averaging the 12-satellite data in groups of four gives 180 epochs, as for 3 satellites, with half the noise per point. The resulting lag uncertainty (@@BINB@@ days) is as small as that of the unbinned 12-satellite data (@@BIN12@@ days) and far below that of the 3-satellite data (@@BIN3@@ days). In the controlled experiment, therefore, the improvement from 3 to 12 satellites is explained by reduced photometric noise and not by the finer sampling interval, as expected for a smooth DRW signal, a 4-day transfer function and 3\% noise.

