\subsection{Photon Budget and Achievable Cadence}
\label{sec:budget}

Table~\ref{tab:budget} gives the per-exposure noise of the representative photometer (120~s exposures). For a 10-cm aperture the continuum channel reaches @@BU10_V14_C@@, @@BU10_V15_C@@, @@BU10_V16_C@@ and @@BU10_V17_C@@ at $V = 14$, 15, 16 and 17, while the 150~\AA\ line channel reaches only @@BU10_V14_L@@ to @@BU10_V17_L@@. Reaching 1\% in the continuum takes @@BU10_V14_T@@, @@BU10_V15_T@@, @@BU10_V16_T@@ and @@BU10_V17_T@@ seconds. A 15-cm aperture lowers the noise by a factor of about 1.5 (@@BU15_V17_C@@ at $V=17$).

\begin{table}[htbp]
